Fix popover closing, nested bookmark dragging, and tab tooltip placement

- Close the Other windows popover, bookmark folder popovers, nested folder submenus, and context menus when an overlay drag crosses its movement threshold. A click without movement does not dismiss them.
- Right-clicking blank space in the Other windows popover offers New tab, New window, and the standard reopen-last-closed action instead of the popover-position menu.
- Right-clicking a popover window header/icon opens the same window context menu as vertical mode. Its Collapse/Expand item reads and updates that popover window's own collapse state.
- Bookmark entries and folders inside root folder popovers and recursively opened submenus carry the same drag metadata as root bookmark items.
- Allow native dragging from bookmark rows in menus and support the existing bookmark-tree reorder handling inside folder popovers and nested folders.
- Add source/drop position feedback to menu-based bookmark entries.
- Position tab tooltips outside the strip: below a top rail, above a bottom rail, right of a left vertical rail, left of a right vertical rail. The Other windows popover and windowed overlay choose the outside side based on their actual position.

Validation: edited JavaScript files pass syntax parsing. No live Chrome UI test was run. Live bookmark synchronization was not changed.
